From 4bf94bdba24d674bfab70b13a9b3e8a496a9ed4c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:50:58 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] test(machine): pin that a machine switch is judged again at
 the post

Trace for #1241: an op generated on machine A, then remounted onto a
machine B whose limits it breaks - through the setup's own machine
(SetSetupMachine) and, separately, the document's (LoadMachine). For
the stroke, the spindle top, a tilting rotary and the machine's kind,
the post re-judges the cached path against B and refuses by name,
writing nothing; undo puts A back and it posts, redo and save/reopen
keep B's refusal. The op stays Ok by the M2.3 roomy-one law (machine
limits are live gate inputs, never stamp inputs), recorded in
docs/decisions/1241-machine-switch-live-gate.md. No product change:
no path cleared on A posts on B unjudged.

Fixes #1241

